---
# Pragmatic level per docs/NAMING.md - Platform/WolfSsl.
#
# Inherits the root .clang-tidy. The pack's public headers refer to upstream
# wolfSSL struct types by forward declaration - `WC_RNG` today, the session and
# context types once the stream lands - because the integrator-supplied handles
# in the config structs are those types. The upstream tags are SCREAMING_CASE
# or `wc_`-prefixed, which violates the project's StructCase + StructPrefix
# rule, but renaming is impossible (they are third-party). Extend
# StructIgnoredRegexp locally so the rule exempts the wolfSSL namespace.
#
# clang-tidy CheckOption values do not merge across the hierarchy - the
# latest-encountered value wins. The pattern below therefore re-states the
# root .clang-tidy whitelist plus the wolfSSL namespace. Keep in sync.
InheritParentConfig: true
CheckOptions:
  - {
      key: readability-identifier-naming.StructIgnoredRegexp,
      value: "^(SolidSyslog|EscapedContext|Gap|LogRequest|OpenHandle|LwipRawDatagramCall|LwipRawDnsResolverCall|LwipRawTcpStreamCall|WC_RNG|WOLFSSL|WOLFSSL_[A-Z0-9_]+|wc_[A-Za-z0-9_]+)$",
    }
